\section{Introduction}

Recent advances in large language models~\citep{lm-4,lm-5,lm-6,llama,llama2,chatgpt,gpt4} have significantly improved the realism of AI-generated text, making it increasingly difficult to distinguish from human-written content. However, this progress also raises concerns about potential misuse, including disinformation dissemination~\citep{woodcock2023wikipedia}, automated phishing~\citep{stokel2022ai}, and academic integrity~\citep{pudasaini2024survey}. In response, detecting LLM-generated text has become an active area of research, with growing interest in techniques for enhancing provenance tracking and content verification.

