\section{Conclusion}
We introduced a general framework for building asymptotically exact variational
families from arbitrary involutive MCMC kernels. By constructing invertible,
measure-preserving maps directly from these kernels, we overcome the main
practical limitation of MixFlow \citep{Xu22mixflow} and enable the construction of 
a broad class of exact flows.
We also provided a streamlined theoretical analysis for flows based on
measure-preserving transformations and demonstrated their empirical advantages
in density approximation and importance sampling.
A promising direction is to pair our framework with recent automatic-tuning MCMC \citep{Liu24,BironLattes24,bou2024gist,bou2024incorporating},
developing truly tuning-free exact flows in practice.


