\section{Detecting Instability}\label{sec:detecting}

The findings in previous sections raise the question of whether LLMs can reliably detect instability in a given matching---a simpler task that involves iterating over each unmatched pair to determine whether both agents prefer one another over their assigned partners.
This procedure requires only a straightforward comparison of preferences and requires $\mathcal{O}(n^2)$ steps.



