The ATT estimates are similar across specifications. This agreement may appear to suggest robustness. However, the theoretical framework developed earlier provides a different interpretation. All three estimators effectively restrict to the same subset of the data—either by design or through implicit weighting. Each is recovering a version of the ATT on the region $X^\ast$, not the full support of $X \mid D = 1$.

Let\[
