\abstract{\noindent
\emph{To a topological groupoid endowed with an involution, we associate a topological groupoid of fixed points, generalizing the fixed-point subspace of a topological space with involution.
We prove that when the topological groupoid with involution arises from a Deligne-Mumford stack over \( \mathbb{R} \), this fixed locus coincides with the real locus of the stack. This provides a topological framework to study real algebraic stacks, and in particular real moduli spaces. Finally, we propose a Smith--Thom type conjecture in this setting, generalizing the Smith--Thom inequality for topological spaces endowed with an involution. 
}
