For an algebraic stack $\ca X$, see \cite[\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06QC}{Tag 06QC}]{stacks-project} for the notions of \emph{gerbe} and \emph{gerbe over an algebraic stack $\ca Y$}. For example, $\ca X$ is a gerbe if there exists an algebraic space $X$ and a morphism $\ca X \to X$ which turns $\ca X$ into a gerbe over $X$. See also \cite[(3.15) -- (3.21), pages 22 -- 24]{laumon-moretbailly}. % see also \cite[\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06QB}{Tag 06QB}]{stacks-project}.
