\begin{proof}[Proof of Proposition \ref{prop:contrexampletoequivariantsmiththom}]

First observe that the elements $\gamma_1 \coloneqq e, \gamma_2 \coloneqq (1 2),\gamma_3 \coloneqq (12)(34) $ form a complete set of representatives of the equivalence classes in $\rm  H^1(G,\mathfrak S_4)$. In particular 
