Before proving Lemma \ref{lem:computationpoincareseries}, let us show that it implies the Proposition \ref{prop:contrexampletoequivariantsmiththom}.
From Lemma \ref{lem:computationpoincareseries} one deduce that
$$\frac{P_{\Gamma^{\gamma_1}}(t)}{P_{\Gamma}(t)}=1\quad \text{and}\quad  \frac{P_{\Gamma^{\gamma_2}}(t)}{P_{\Gamma}(t)}=\frac{1+t+t^2}{1+t^2}=\frac{P_{\Gamma^{\gamma_3}}(t)}{P_{\Gamma}(t)},$$
so that, combined with (\ref{eq:cardinalityH^1S4}), one has 
$$\frac{h^*([X/\Gamma])}{h^*([X/\Gamma]_{\mathbb C})}=\frac{(1+3/2+3/2)}{3}=\frac{4}{3},$$
which what we wanted. We are left to show Lemma \ref{lem:computationpoincareseries}.
