We notice here that the blow-up equation already determines at this stage the analogue of the previous integration constant $c_{1}$, for the $m_{2}=2$ functions. Using the value of $g_{1,2}'(0)$ to simplify the equation, we can solve it for $\tilde{g}_{2,1}(x)$ obtaining:
