Then, the sixth equation for $m_{1}=2$ reads:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\frac{1}{300} \left(-143 + 21312\, g_{1,3}'(0) + 2160\, \tilde{g}_{1,3}'(0) \right) + \left(-\frac{55}{432} + 19\, g_{1,3}'(0) + 2\, \tilde{g}_{1,3}'(0) \right) x \\
&+ \left(-\frac{14161}{1296} + 16\, g_{3,2}'(0) + 4\, \tilde{f}_{3,2}''(0) \right) x^2 + \frac{5}{36} \left(-16 + 72\, g_{2,2}^{(3)}(0) + 3\, \tilde{f}_{2,2}^{(4)}(0) \right) x^4 \\
&+ \left( g_{1,2}^{(5)}(0) + \frac{1}{60} \left( -15 + \tilde{f}_{1,2}^{(6)}(0) \right) \right) x^6=0,
