\section{Conclusion}
\label{Conclusion}
In this work, we propose a novel sampling theory in the JFRFT domain, enhancing the expressive power of signal representations in time-frequency analysis and GSP. By establishing the conditions for perfect recovery of jointly bandlimited signals and developing optimal sampling set selection strategies, we construct a unified JFRFT-based sampling framework. Multiple sampling strategies are proposed and systematically compared within this framework. To further improve the efficiency of large-scale joint time-vertex signal processing, we investigate the design of localized sampling operators and integrate them with the proposed strategies. Numerical experiments demonstrate the superior reconstruction accuracy and computational efficiency of our methods, offering a new paradigm for efficient processing of time-varying graph signals.


