GPT-4o-mini (version 2024-07-18) for all experiments, and also included Llama 3.2 3B to evaluate performance in limited-resource settings.
While GPT-4o-mini is a larger, high-performing model, Llama 3.2 3B is an open-source alternative with fewer parameters (3 billion) and reduced computational requirements. By including Llama in our experiments, we aim to demonstrate the effectiveness and generalizability of our method even when deployed with smaller, more accessible language models. 


\subsection{Data Reduction}
Table~\ref{tab:data_reduction} highlights the efficiency of our model in reducing data size by focusing only on relevant attributes. Unlike other methods that use all available attributes, such as FMW, our approach selects a smaller set of dependent attributes identified in the initial phase. This targeted selection leads to a significant reduction in the amount of data processed, as shown by the lower character counts across all datasets. 
The reduction in characters is computed by comparing the average length of the selected attributes to that of all attributes. The effect is substantial across all benchmarks: in the Zomato dataset, character input is reduced by 95.7\% through the selection of only 2 out of 16 attributes. Similarly, the Buy, Restaurant, and Phone achieve reductions of 57.1\%, 39.9\%, and 74.0\%, respectively. 
As a result, the process becomes more explainable and the outcomes more traceable, since it is easier to understand which attributes contribute to the final results.

