Now a truncation argument is needed for later use. Note that \eqref{eqZ_N} can be seen as an equation for $Z_N$ {\em given} the process $Y_N$. Actually, for a given process $\tY_N$ and after having extended by setting $f(x) = 0$ for $x<0$, the corresponding solution $\tZ_N$ can be obtained pathwise, i.e. given the jumps of the processes $n_i^{\pm}$. In particular, for a fixed $h>0$, we choose $\tY_N(t) := Y_N(t) \wedge h$. Note that $\tZ_N(t) = Z_N(t)$ up to the stopping time 
\[
\tau^N_h := \inf\{t>0 : Y_N(t) > h\}.
\]
We have 
\be{eqtZ_N}
\begin{split}
\tZ_N(t) & = E_N + F_N t  - \a \sqrt{N} \int_0^{t} \tZ_N(s) ds \\ & ~~~~~~+ \frac{1-\g}{2 \sqrt{N}} \int_{[0,\sqrt{N} t]} {\bf 1}_{[0,\tilde{\l}_N^+(s))}(u) \sum_{i=1}^N n_i^+(ds,du) - \frac{1-\g}{2 \sqrt{N}} \int_{[0,\sqrt{N} t]} {\bf 1}_{[0,\tilde{\l}_N^-(s))}(u) \sum_{i=1}^N n_i^-(ds,du),
