\subsubsection{Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)}
\label{se:PPO}

The Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) algorithm (see \cite{Schulman2017PPO}) has been developed with the objective of reducing the variance of the policy updates. It is an actor-critic algorithm which clips what is called the \textit{probability ratio}, a measure of how far the new policy is from the previous policy, and thus penalizes large updates to the policy so as to reduce the variance of updates and prevent the policy from performing catastrophic updates.
